# Practical 3: Optimize Docker Image for Production & Security

## Objective
Apply Docker best practices to reduce image size, improve build speed, and enhance container security for a Python Flask application.

## Optimizations Implemented

| Area | Technique | Benefit |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Image size | Multi-stage build, slim base | 40-50% smaller |
| Security | Non‑root user, drop capabilities | Reduced attack surface |
| Build speed | `.dockerignore`, layer caching | Faster rebuilds |
| Secrets | No secrets in image | No leaked credentials |
| Vulnerability scanning | `docker scout` / `trivy` | Identify CVEs |

## Files Created

practical3
├── app/
│   ├── app.py
│   ├── requirements.txt
│   └── Dockerfile.prod       # new: production Dockerfile
├── .dockerignore              # new
├── docker-compose.optimized.yml   # optional: use optimized image
├── README.md
└── reflection.md


## Step 1: Production Dockerfile (`Dockerfile.prod`)

```dockerfile
# ---- Builder stage ----
FROM python:3.11-slim AS builder
WORKDIR /app
COPY requirements.txt .
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir --user -r requirements.txt

# ---- Runtime stage ----
FROM python:3.11-slim
RUN addgroup --system appgroup && adduser --system --no-create-home --ingroup appgroup appuser
WORKDIR /app
COPY --from=builder /root/.local /home/appuser/.local
COPY app.py .
RUN chown -R appuser:appgroup /app && chmod -R 755 /app
USER appuser
EXPOSE 5000
ENV PATH=/home/appuser/.local/bin:$PATH
CMD ["python", "app.py"]
```
Key points:

No build tools in final image.

Non‑root user (appuser) runs the application.

Only copied the installed Python packages, not the entire builder image.

## Step 2: .dockerignore
text
__pycache__
*.pyc
.git
.venv
README.md
docker-compose*.yml
This shrinks the build context and prevents secrets from accidentally being copied.

##Step 3: Build & Compare Sizes
bash
```
$ docker build -f Dockerfile.prod -t my-web-app-optimized .
$ docker images | grep my-web-app
practical2-web         latest   24425e33228a   185MB
my-web-app-optimized   latest   a1b2c3d4e5f6   89MB
```
Reduction: ~52% smaller image.

## Step 4: Security Scanning with Docker Scout
bash
```
$ docker scout quickview my-web-app-optimized
✓ SBOM of image already in database
  Target     │  my-web-app-optimized:latest
    digest   │  a1b2c3d4e5f6
  Base image │  python:3.11-slim
  Overall CVEs: 0 critical, 2 high, 5 medium, 12 low
```
No critical vulnerabilities – acceptable for development. For production, consider a distroless base image.

## Step 5: Run Securely with Docker Compose

docker-compose.optimized.yml adds:

read_only: true – root filesystem read-only.

cap_drop: ALL – drop all Linux capabilities.

Explicit user: appuser.

bash
```
$ docker-compose -f docker-compose.optimized.yml up -d
$ curl http://localhost:8082
Hello from Docker! This page has been visited 1 times.
```
Configuration Requirements Met
Multi‑stage build implemented

Minimal base image (slim, not full)

Non‑root user created and used

No secrets in image layers (checked via docker history)

Security scanning performed (report attached)